      history: 'Cauterization for hemostasis dates to ancient civilizations using heated metal instruments. The development of electrically heated wire cautery began in the early 20th century with the introduction of battery-powered heated platinum loops. Modern portable electrocautery units with temperature control and disposable tips were developed in the 1970s, providing precise and controlled thermal coagulation.',
