      clinicalImportance: 'Proper patient positioning is critical for surgical success and patient safety. The operating table enables the surgeon to achieve optimal exposure of the surgical site through various positions (supine, prone, lateral, Trendelenburg, lithotomy). Incorrect positioning can lead to pressure injuries, nerve damage, compartment syndrome, impaired ventilation, or inadequate surgical access, making the operating table a critical component of surgical safety.',
