      clinicalImportance: 'Surgical navigation has transformed complex procedures by enabling minimally invasive approaches, reducing surgical time, minimizing tissue damage, and improving surgical accuracy. In neurosurgery, it allows precise tumor resection while preserving eloquent cortex. In spinal surgery, it guides pedicle screw placement with high accuracy, reducing malposition rates. In ENT, it enables safe endoscopic sinus surgery by tracking instruments relative to critical structures like the orbit and skull base.',
